        "text": "Now we have a general idea of what a blockchain is and how it works, but what can it actually be used for? Let's review some of the important fields where blockchain technology is being utilized. Sending money between different parts of the world can be quite expensive, with middlemen charging hefty fees for what's essentially moving bits around on the Internet. How would you react if it suddenly took three working days to send an email? While sending money is a more delicate matter than sending an email, the remittance infrastructure is undoubtedly outdated. Sending money via blockchain can be fast and incur low fees. Many countries have or are considering issuing central bank digital currency, also known as cbdc. It's the digital form of a country's fiat currency. This could have a huge impact on the remittance market and the global financial services market.",
